   "stem": {
      "text": "The position of a particle moving along a line is s(t) meters at time t seconds. Selected values of s(t) are given in the table. Compute the average rate of change of s over each of the intervals \\( [5, 5.100] \\), \\( [5, 5.010] \\), \\( [5, 5.001] \\), and use them to find the rate at which s is changing at \\( t = 5 \\). Indicate units of measure.",
      "command_verb": "estimate"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -31,
      "units": "meters per second"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The average rate over \\( [5, 5 + h] \\) is \\( \\frac{s(5 + h) - s(5)}{h} \\), which for h = 0.1, 0.01 and 0.001 gives -31.300, -31.030, -31.003.",
         "rule_named": "average rate of change"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As the intervals shrink the averages approach -31, so the instantaneous rate at \\( t = 5 \\) is -31 meters per second. Each average is only an approximation of it.",
         "mathjson": -31,
         "rule_named": "instantaneous rate as the limit of average rates"
      }
   ],
